1
00:00:07,130 --> 00:00:09,673
Whiskers and the Stroke of Four.

2
00:00:22,351 --> 00:00:26,121
One grey morning, the old radio crackled to life.

3
00:00:29,440 --> 00:00:34,918
This is London. And when Big Ben strikes four, all of London stops... for tea.

4
00:00:35,118 --> 00:00:37,833
Big Ben! I want to hear it bong with my own ears!

5
00:00:38,033 --> 00:00:40,520
Did somebody say tea? With cakes?

6
00:00:40,720 --> 00:00:44,326
London is across the sea, Luna. Cats don't swim.

7
00:00:50,765 --> 00:00:53,722
Royal Air Mail, coming through! Any post for London?

8
00:00:53,922 --> 00:00:56,125
Us! Can you post two cats to London?

9
00:00:56,325 --> 00:00:59,819
Hop in, my dears! If the wind is kind, we'll land before four.

10
00:01:06,258 --> 00:01:11,030
So the balloon floated up, over the fields and over the sea, to England.

11
00:01:18,361 --> 00:01:22,182
I'm not scared. I'm keeping my eyes shut on purpose.

12
00:01:25,947 --> 00:01:29,158
Excuse me, is this the bag for London? Because I'm in it!

13
00:01:29,358 --> 00:01:30,614
Pip! You came too!

14
00:01:37,944 --> 00:01:41,614
There's London! The Thames, Tower Bridge, the London Eye... and the rain.

15
00:01:41,814 --> 00:01:45,350
I've letters to deliver. Meet me at Big Ben at four o'clock!

16
00:01:50,897 --> 00:01:54,877
London was wet. Very wet. And cats do not like wet.

17
00:01:55,077 --> 00:01:59,560
My fur! My beautiful fur! Is there anywhere dry in this city?

18
00:02:08,673 --> 00:02:10,961
Excuse me, sir. Which way is Big Ben?

19
00:02:15,617 --> 00:02:17,687
Is he a statue? Hello? Boo!

20
00:02:17,887 --> 00:02:22,103
I am a King's Guard. Guards do not wiggle, giggle, or chat.

21
00:02:22,303 --> 00:02:27,042
But Big Ben is that way. And the best fish and chips are by the river.

22
00:02:27,242 --> 00:02:29,890
Fish? And chips? Sir, you are my hero.

23
00:02:35,438 --> 00:02:40,735
The rain stopped. And by the river, Whiskers found heaven, wrapped in paper.

24
00:02:40,935 --> 00:02:44,486
Hello, my lovely chips. Hello, my lovely fish.

25
00:02:52,707 --> 00:02:54,998
Ta very much, ginger!

26
00:02:55,198 --> 00:02:57,558
Hey! Thief! Come back with my fish!

27
00:03:12,019 --> 00:03:15,736
Whiskers, this bus is going the wrong way! Big Ben is behind us!

28
00:03:15,936 --> 00:03:18,987
Nobody steals a cat's fish. Nobody!

29
00:03:23,643 --> 00:03:26,132
Look at the clock! It's half past three already!

30
00:03:37,027 --> 00:03:39,509
Aha! Got you, you feathery... oh.

31
00:03:44,166 --> 00:03:48,623
Sorry, mate. The rain stopped my fishing, and my little ones were starving.

32
00:03:53,280 --> 00:03:56,961
Here. Have the fish. Have all of it. They need it more than me.

33
00:03:57,161 --> 00:03:58,749
Whiskers, that was so kind.

34
00:04:02,514 --> 00:04:04,971
The bridge is going up! And it's nearly four!

35
00:04:05,171 --> 00:04:07,063
We'll never get to Big Ben in time.

36
00:04:07,263 --> 00:04:11,388
Never say never to a seagull! Oi, lads! Fetch that balloon!

37
00:04:24,066 --> 00:04:26,882
Hold on to your whiskers! Next stop, Big Ben!

38
00:04:43,126 --> 00:04:45,243
I heard it! With my very own ears!

39
00:04:49,008 --> 00:04:53,245
At four o'clock, high above London, everybody stopped for tea.

40
00:04:53,445 --> 00:04:57,575
Scones! Jam! Cream! Is it four o'clock every day here?

41
00:04:57,775 --> 00:05:00,857
You're alright, ginger. Sorry about your fish.

42
00:05:01,057 --> 00:05:04,020
I gave it away. Completely on purpose.

43
00:05:17,589 --> 00:05:22,432
That night, the Royal Air Mail delivered two very special parcels home.

44
00:05:27,980 --> 00:05:29,668
Where shall we go next, Whiskers?

45
00:05:29,868 --> 00:05:31,798
Anywhere that stops for tea.

46
00:05:36,455 --> 00:05:42,322
Because being kind might make you a little bit late. But it is never, ever the wrong time.

